            "t": "p",
            "text": "Hans Ørberg’s Rōma Aeterna follows Quintilian’s plan. The book begins with Ørberg’s own admirable prose (Caps. XXXVI to XL). Cap. XXXVI helps the instructor assess student strengths and weaknesses. This chapter effortlessly brings students back to their Latin after the inevitable break from Latin over summer or winter vacations. It also introduces critical new syntax. Students"
